---
import PracticeAreaLayout from '../../layouts/PracticeAreaLayout.astro';
---

<PracticeAreaLayout
  title="Workers' Rights Legal Help | Maine Volunteer Lawyers Project"
  description="VLP's Workers' Rights Legal Clinic provides free legal advice to low-income Maine workers on harassment, discrimination, and unpaid wages."
  heading="Workers' Rights & Employment"
  intro="Free legal advice for low-income Maine workers on harassment, discrimination, unpaid wages, and other workplace legal matters."
  ctaHeading="Ready to get help with your workers' rights case?"
  ctaText="Complete an online intake form to request a clinic appointment. VLP staff will review your submission and follow up with you."
>

  <div slot="body">

    <h2>About Workers' Rights</h2>
    <p>
      Employment law issues can be difficult to navigate alone. VLP provides
      free legal advice to low-income Maine workers to help them understand
      their rights and assess potential legal claims. The clinic can assist with:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Workplace harassment</li>
      <li>Discrimination</li>
      <li>Unpaid wages</li>
      <li>Other employment law matters</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This program originated through collaboration with the Southern Maine
      Workers' Center.
    </p>

    <h2>About This Clinic</h2>

    <div class="notice-box">
      <p>
        Services are free with income-based eligibility. To request an
        appointment, complete the online intake form. A VLP staff member will
        follow up within one to two weeks. If you have an upcoming court date
        or deadline, please note it in your submission.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      The Workers' Rights Legal Clinic operates twice each month on a remote
      basis. Employment law specialists assist low-income workers in
      understanding their workplace rights and assessing potential legal claims.
    </p>

    <h2>Additional Resources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://maineworkers.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Southern Maine Workers' Center</a>
         -  works to improve working conditions and employment terms for working-class and low-income people in Maine
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://maine.gov/labor" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Maine Department of Labor</a>
         -  committed to safe and fair workplaces for Maine workers and businesses
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://maine.freelegalanswers.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Free Legal Answers Maine</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://ptla.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pine Tree Legal Assistance</a>
      </li>
    </ul>

  </div>

  <div slot="sidebar">

    <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-card--info">
      <h3>Eligibility</h3>
      <ul class="sidebar-list">
        <li>Maine legal matter or Maine court</li>
        <li>Limited income (generally at or below 200% of federal poverty level)</li>
        <li>Civil legal matter (not a criminal charge)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-card--info">
      <h3>About This Clinic</h3>
      <ul class="sidebar-list">
        <li>Held twice each month</li>
        <li>Remote  -  online or by phone</li>
        <li>Employment law specialists</li>
        <li>Free of charge</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-card--info">
      <h3>Topics Covered</h3>
      <ul class="sidebar-list">
        <li>Workplace harassment</li>
        <li>Discrimination</li>
        <li>Unpaid wages</li>
        <li>Other employment matters</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>

</PracticeAreaLayout>
